{"id":"u-19568d27-8352-4106-9219-070f90baa949","src":"community","title":"PPL-UL July 2026","author":"Colton L.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/8E7ew8-ppl-ul-july-2026","desc":"Basic powerbuilding program for intermediate-advanced lifters. Bodybuilding on the top, powerlifting on the bottom. Styled as 5/3/1 PRO+Jokers+FSL for squat and deadlift.\n\nUse 90% of your actual 1RM for your Training Max... put that number in for your 1RM at the beginning of the program.\n\nLower-body compounds explained:\nDo the written sets as they are. If everything feels good, do doubles and/or singles, increasing weight (by 20lbs per set for squat, by 30lbs per set for deadlift) until the bar gets really slow. Only singles beyond 90% of actual 1RM (not TM). Probably only singles for all Joker Sets for deadlift, your call. After the Joker Sets, do FSL (stands for First Set Last, meaning the weight that you used for the first set) for the sets/reps listed in the notes.\n\nIf you're comfortable, add 10 lbs to your training max at the end of the cycle. \n\nThe rest is to get pretty. I added lateral raises onto my leg days because I want boulder shoulders and delts only need 48 hours to recover, but those could be omitted I guess.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-13T23:12:01.156Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Pull","Legs","Upper","Lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":9,"rpe":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Viking Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":6}]},{"n":"Single Arm Overhead Tricep Extension","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":6}]}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8